+assertions and authority records stay exact. The exact reviewed #533 C27 patch is
+reused without additional modification. No operational adapter/helper is repinned.
+
+Five NEW explicit fixture/TEST metadata forwards are proposed: retained producer,
+retained consumer, provider output test, C14 output test and C27 output test. They
+map only exact current bytes to immutable c60 source-check bytes. Both fixed S
+output files always remain actual S source. The other five phase endpoints (two
+joint header hashes, retained producer, retained consumer and C27 source) must be
+all original or all proposed; partial, stale and mixed states deny.
+
+These five internal metadata reads use the existing seven ports' bounded-call
+model: a fresh complete physical tree/sole-parent/author proof before and after
+every public qualification/exported-helper operation; fresh actual disk/callback
+body, mode and immutable historical bytes on EACH projection. No source-success
+cache crosses calls. Direct readCurrent for only these five runs checked full
+pre/post proofs; unknown/outside read paths deny. The approved P1 TEST port remains
+unchanged and independently runs a fresh full physical proof on EVERY P1 read.
+Actual test execution always reads the corrected files on disk, never this view.
+
+All old seven historical ports, P1 port, original two historical snapshots and
+original2+39 assertion bodies/budgets remain exact. Both joint header hashes reseal
+together. No new wrapper, namespace, engine, general source fallback or runtime
+capability is added. The manifest seals README/controls, the helper seals the
+manifest, and generated source headers seal the helper. Store current final hashes
+and qualification reports outside these companions to avoid self-reference.
